    "text": "Electrophile attack where the electron density high.which shows +M or +I effects are ortho/para directing because they increase electron density at ortho and para +M&nbsp; &nbsp;<math><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mtext>N</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>•</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>•</mo></mrow></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mtext>N</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>•</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>•</mo></mrow></mover><mo>=</mo><mtext>O</mtext><mo>,</mo></math> <img src=\"assets\\st0035_c6f5f8c97688.png\" style=\"width:0.98792in;height:0.4649in\" />, <img src=\"assets\\st0035_d7d13e135e88.png\" style=\"width:1in;height:0.41772in\" />, <img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0035_598cd90d8b64.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 33px;\" /><br />The following groups are meta directing <img src=\"assets\\st0035_ffa237353543.png\" style=\"width:0.57297in;height:0.45755in\" /> ,<img src=\"assets\\st0035_67321c272259.png\" style=\"width:0.58977in;height:0.43844in\" />, <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> They decreases electron density at ortho/para so, electrophile attack at meta position."
